  "context": {
    "client_id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-c10000000001",
    "notes": [
      "a permanent rejection ⇒ a rejected verdict, never a queue wedge (P:verdict-completeness-transforms-and-conflict-rejection, D-rejection-reasons): the same defensive floor RLS_DENIED and PRECONDITION get (push/002, push/004); a permanent reject dead-letters (the client surfaces it and clears the outbox entry), it never blocks or retries the queue",
      "mutation f...006 targets pk row-3, a row this client's outbox references but the server has no record of: never inserted, never tombstoned; a non-insert op against such a row yields RLS_DENIED because an RLS-scoped server cannot (and must not) distinguish 'absent' from 'RLS-hidden' without leaking existence, the existence oracle it must not reintroduce (D-rejection-reasons); the class-23 CONSTRAINT literal stays reserved for a genuine in-transaction integrity failure",
      "the second mutation in the same unflagged batch (an ordinary edit to the owned, existing row-1) still applies: head-of-line is never blocked (P:outbox-and-serial-in-flight); the typed MUTATION_REJECTED event surfaces the loss (DX:offline-writes)"
    ],
